      "name": "Amanoiwato Shrine",
      "description": "Amanoiwato Shrine venerates the sacred cave where, according to Japanese mythology, the sun goddess Amaterasu hid herself, plunging the world into darkness until lured out by the other gods. The cave itself is across the river and can be viewed with shrine staff escort. The shrine's peaceful forest setting exudes a profound spiritual atmosphere.",
